STAR OCEAN: anamnesis on the desktop: {{IF port}}the desktop port of 3.7.0{{END}}{{IF emulator}}the 3.7.0 emulator and its local server{{END}}{{IF viewer}}the offline client in soa-viewer{{END}}
Version {{VERSION}} ({{PLATFORM}}), built from commit {{COMMIT}}
==========================================================================
{{IF viewer}}
soa-viewer{{EXE}} runs the offline build of STAR OCEAN: anamnesis (JP), the version released after{{# 380-ok}}
the online service ended, unmodified, in an emulator: the game as a phone shows it today (no
server). Your progress stays on this computer.

This package holds no game files. You supply your own copy of the game (below); soa-viewer reads
it where it is and never changes it.


1. Game files
-------------

soa-viewer needs one file: the offline game's XAPK as downloaded from APKPure,{{# 380-ok}}
  STAR+OCEAN+-anamnesis-_3.8.0_APKPure.xapk{{# 380-ok: soa-viewer's game file}}
Any file name ending in .xapk works when it holds the game (soa-viewer reads it in place, without{{# 380-ok}}
unpacking it). Put it in the folder "game" beside soa-viewer{{EXE}} (it is already there, empty):

  {{TOP}}/
    soa-viewer{{EXE}}
{{IF windows}}
    run-viewer.cmd
{{ELSE}}
    run-viewer.sh
{{END}}
    README.txt  (this file)
    game/
      STAR+OCEAN+-anamnesis-_3.8.0_APKPure.xapk{{# 380-ok: soa-viewer's game file}}

It may also sit directly beside soa-viewer{{EXE}} instead of in game/.

Where soa-viewer looks, first match wins:
  1. the command-line flags (below);
  2. a source checkout of the project, when it runs from one (developers);
  3. the folder soa-viewer{{EXE}} is stored in (not the current directory);
  4. its game/ subfolder.
In 3. and 4. only the top level is searched: the first *.xapk there that holds the game.{{# 380-ok}}


2. Running
----------

{{IF windows}}
  Double-click run-viewer.cmd, or in a terminal:  soa-viewer.exe [options]
{{ELSE}}
  ./soa-viewer [options]        (or ./run-viewer.sh [options])
{{END}}

soa-viewer{{EXE}}
  needs:      the offline game's XAPK (1.){{# 380-ok}}
  flags:      --xapk FILE          the XAPK{{# 380-ok}}
              --apk-dir DIR        the XAPK unpacked instead (its APKs in DIR){{# 380-ok}}
              --data DIR           where the game's data and save go (default below)
              --fullscreen, --size WxH, --landscape, ...  soa-viewer{{EXE}} --help lists them all.
  writes to:  {{IF windows}}%LOCALAPPDATA%\soa\viewer-380\{{ELSE}}~/.local/share/soa-viewer-380/{{END}}  (unless --data DIR): the phone's data and
              save, libSOA.so (taken from the XAPK on the first run), the asset pack's files{{# 380-ok}}


3. The first run
----------------

soa-viewer takes the client library (libSOA.so) out of the XAPK into its data dir, once (a{{# 380-ok}}
second; again only when the XAPK's library changes), and installs the asset pack's files there.{{# 380-ok}}


4. When something is missing
----------------------------

soa-viewer stops with a message naming the file and where it looked:

  fatal: the 3.8.0 XAPK wasn't found: give --xapk FILE (or put the *.xapk in <here>/game, beside{{# 380-ok: soa-viewer's message}}
         soa-viewer, or in the repository's apk/: see README.txt), or --apk-dir DIR

Put the file as in 1. and start again.


5. What is in this package
--------------------------

  soa-viewer{{EXE}}           the program (optimized build, debug info stripped: a separate
                              debug-symbols zip of the same version has it)
  LICENSE.txt                 this software's license (GNU GPL v3)
  THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt     the licenses of the libraries it links
  BUILD-INFO.txt              the version, commit and build settings

{{IF linux}}
Linux needs: glibc 2.39 or newer (Ubuntu 24.04, Debian 13, Fedora 40 or later), libEGL and
libGLESv2 (Mesa: libegl1, libgles2, libegl-mesa0, libgl1-mesa-dri), X11 or Wayland, PulseAudio
or PipeWire (pipewire-pulse) for sound, ffmpeg for the story movies, and a Japanese font for
the name-entry box (e.g. fonts-ipaexfont-gothic or fonts-noto-cjk).
{{ELSE}}
Windows needs: Windows 10 or 11 (x64). Everything else is built in, except ffmpeg for the story
movies: put ffmpeg.exe beside the program or on PATH (without it the movies do not play).
{{END}}
{{ELSE}}
{{IF port}}
soa{{EXE}} is the desktop port of the last online client of STAR OCEAN: anamnesis (3.7.0, JP),
with a local game server built in: no network and no account needed. Your progress stays on
this computer.
{{ELSE}}
soa-emu{{EXE}} runs the original 3.7.0 client of STAR OCEAN: anamnesis (JP), unmodified, in an
emulator; soa-server{{EXE}} is the local game server it talks to (it can also run on its own, for
any client that connects to it). run-emulator{{IF windows}}.cmd{{ELSE}}.sh{{END}} starts the server, then the client, and stops
the server when you close the client.
{{END}}

This package holds no game files. You supply your own copy of the game (below); the programs read
it where it is and never change it.


1. Game files
-------------

You need two files:

  STAR+OCEAN+-anamnesis-_3.7.0_APKPure.apk
      the 3.7.0 app (APK). Any file name ending in .apk works: the programs recognise the
      3.7.0 APK by its contents (lib/arm64-v8a/libSOA.so of 3.7.0); other versions are skipped
      with a note in the log.

  SOA-3.7.0-canonical-data.zip
      the full 3.7.0 download (the data the online game downloaded: version.bin, manifest/,
      sqlite/, Sound/, Character/, ...). Leave it zipped, or extract it into a folder (any name);
      a folder counts when it holds version.bin, manifest/ and sqlite/basmaster.sqlite3.

Put them in the folder "game" beside the program{{IF windows}}s{{END}} (it is already there, empty), like this:

  {{TOP}}/
{{IF port}}
    soa{{EXE}}
{{IF windows}}
    run-port.cmd
{{ELSE}}
    run-port.sh
{{END}}
{{ELSE}}
    soa-emu{{EXE}}
    soa-server{{EXE}}
{{IF windows}}
    run-emulator.cmd, run-emulator.ps1
{{ELSE}}
    run-emulator.sh
{{END}}
{{END}}
    README.txt  (this file)
    data/  standin-assets/  (ours: see 5.)
    game/
      STAR+OCEAN+-anamnesis-_3.7.0_APKPure.apk
      SOA-3.7.0-canonical-data.zip          <- or the extracted folder, e.g. game/download-3.7.0/

They may also sit directly beside the program instead of in game/.

Where the programs look, first match wins:
  1. the command-line flags (below);
  2. a source checkout of the project, when the program runs from one (developers);
  3. the folder the program is stored in (not the current directory);
  4. its game/ subfolder.
In 3. and 4. only the top level is searched: the APK is any *.apk there, the data is
SOA-3.7.0-canonical-data.zip there, or a folder there (or the folder itself) holding the download.


2. Running
----------

{{IF port}}
{{IF windows}}
  Double-click run-port.cmd, or in a terminal:  soa.exe [options]
{{ELSE}}
  ./soa [options]        (or ./run-port.sh [options])
{{END}}

soa{{EXE}}
  needs:      the 3.7.0 APK and the 3.7.0 download (1.)
  flags:      --apk FILE           the APK
              --download PATH      the download: SOA-3.7.0-canonical-data.zip or a folder
                                   (--download-dir DIR is the same)
              --master FILE        an already decrypted 3.7.0 master DB (normally not needed: 3.)
              --data DIR           where your save and the server's state go (default below)
              --fullscreen, --size WxH, --new-player, --seed FILE, --enable-events, ...
              soa{{EXE}} --help lists them all.
  writes to:  {{IF windows}}%LOCALAPPDATA%\soa\port-370\{{ELSE}}~/.local/share/soa-linux-370/{{END}}  (unless --data DIR):
              the phone's data and save, server.sqlite3 (your player), libSOA-3.7.0.so (taken from
              the APK on the first run), master/ (the master DB, 3.), cdn/ (the local CDN's cache)
{{ELSE}}
{{IF windows}}
  Double-click run-emulator.cmd, or in a terminal:  run-emulator.cmd [options]
{{ELSE}}
  ./run-emulator.sh [options]
{{END}}
  Options: --new-player (start a fresh account), --seed FILE (start from a 3.7.0 or offline
  Game.xml), --enable-events, --port N, --home DIR; others go to soa-emu (e.g. --fullscreen).
  run-emulator{{IF windows}}.cmd{{ELSE}}.sh{{END}} --help lists them.
  Data: {{IF windows}}%LOCALAPPDATA%\soa\emulator-370\{{ELSE}}~/.local/share/soa-emulator-370/{{END}}  (unless --home DIR): phone{{IF windows}}\{{ELSE}}/{{END}} (the
  client's data and save), server{{IF windows}}\{{ELSE}}/{{END}} (the server's state, master{{IF windows}}\{{ELSE}}/{{END}}, cdn{{IF windows}}\{{ELSE}}/{{END}}), server.log.

soa-server{{EXE}}
  needs:      the 3.7.0 download (1.): it serves it to the client (the local CDN) and decrypts
              the game's master DB from it (3.). The APK is not needed.
  flags:      --download PATH      the download: SOA-3.7.0-canonical-data.zip or a folder
                                   (--download-dir DIR is the same)
              --master FILE        an already decrypted 3.7.0 master DB
              --data DIR           its state (server.sqlite3), master/, cdn/ (run-emulator passes
                                   HOME{{IF windows}}\{{ELSE}}/{{END}}server; without --data: ./server.sqlite3, and the master under
                                   {{IF windows}}%LOCALAPPDATA%\soa\server-370\master{{ELSE}}~/.local/share/soa-server-370/master{{END}})
              --listen HOST:PORT   the game port (default 127.0.0.1:44300); --http HOST:PORT the
                                   CDN (default 127.0.0.1:44380); soa-server{{EXE}} --help lists all
  Without a download it still answers the game, but has no CDN: the client can't get its data.

soa-emu{{EXE}}
  needs:      the 3.7.0 APK (1.). It gets the rest of the data from soa-server, like the real
              game did (the first start downloads about 3 GB from it into the phone's data).
  flags:      --apk FILE           the APK
              --data DIR           the phone's data (default {{IF windows}}%LOCALAPPDATA%\soa\emulator-370\phone{{ELSE}}~/.local/share/soa-emulator-370/phone{{END}})
              --server HOST:PORT, --http HOST:PORT   where soa-server listens
              soa-emu{{EXE}} --help lists them all.
  writes to:  the phone's data dir: the client's files and save, libSOA-3.7.0.so (taken from the
              APK on the first run)
{{END}}


3. The first run
----------------

The programs prepare what they need from your game files, once:
  - the client library libSOA.so is taken out of the APK into the data dir (a second);
  - the game's master database is decrypted from the download's sqlite/basmaster.sqlite3 into
    the data dir's master/ folder (a few seconds). Its file name holds a hash of the source, so a
    different download is decrypted again; nothing else changes the cached copy. Without a
    download, the APK's built-in master is used as a last resort (it is older: some content is
    missing; a warning says so), but the local CDN still needs the download;
  - the local CDN indexes the download (cdn/; seconds from a fast disk, up to a minute from a
    slow one; zipped or extracted makes no difference).
{{IF emulator}}
  - soa-emu's client then downloads its data from soa-server (about 3 GB, a few minutes), as the
    real game did on a phone.
{{END}}


4. When something is missing
----------------------------

The program stops with a message naming the file, and where it looked, for example:

{{IF port}}
  fatal: the 3.7.0 APK wasn't found (--apk FILE, ...); put the game files in <here>/game
         (the 3.7.0 APK, and the 3.7.0 download: SOA-3.7.0-canonical-data.zip, zipped or extracted): see README.txt
  fatal: --server inproc needs the 3.7.0 download: give --download PATH (a folder or
         SOA-3.7.0-canonical-data.zip; ...); put the game files in ...
{{ELSE}}
  soa-emu:    fatal: the 3.7.0 APK wasn't found (give --apk); put the game files in <here>/game ...
  soa-server: E/server: no 3.7.0 master DB: give --master FILE, or --download-dir DIR (the 3.7.0
              download, ...; a folder or SOA-3.7.0-canonical-data.zip), or put the game files in ...
  run-emulator: soa-server found no 3.7.0 download (see README.txt); log: .../server.log
{{END}}

An APK of another version is skipped with "another version of the game (its libSOA.so isn't
3.7.0's)" in the log. Put the files as in 1. and start again.


5. What is in this package
--------------------------

{{IF port}}
  soa{{EXE}}                  the program (optimized build, debug info stripped: a separate
                              debug-symbols zip of the same version has it)
{{ELSE}}
  soa-emu{{EXE}}, soa-server{{EXE}}   the programs (optimized builds, debug info stripped: a separate
                              debug-symbols zip of the same version has it)
{{END}}
  data/gacha_pools.sqlite3    our reconstruction of the gacha draw pools (ids and rates; the gacha
                              titles come from your master at run time)
  data/saves/seed/Game.xml    the server's default starting player (a 3.7.0 end-of-service save,
                              its player id replaced): the state of a new local server unless
                              --new-player or --seed FILE
  standin-assets/             made-up stand-in images (marked "STAND-IN") for banners the online
                              server had already deleted
  LICENSE.txt                 this software's license (GNU GPL v3)
  THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt     the licenses of the libraries it links
  BUILD-INFO.txt              the version, commit and build settings

{{IF linux}}
Linux needs: glibc 2.39 or newer (Ubuntu 24.04, Debian 13, Fedora 40 or later), libEGL and
libGLESv2 (Mesa: libegl1, libgles2, libegl-mesa0, libgl1-mesa-dri), X11 or Wayland, PulseAudio
or PipeWire (pipewire-pulse) for sound, ffmpeg for the story movies, and a Japanese font for
the name-entry box (e.g. fonts-ipaexfont-gothic or fonts-noto-cjk).
{{ELSE}}
Windows needs: Windows 10 or 11 (x64). Everything else is built in, except ffmpeg for the story
movies: put ffmpeg.exe beside the program or on PATH (without it the movies do not play).
{{END}}
{{END}}
